00:01:25.205 --> 00:01:26.660
- Pop music.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:30.060
We have a lot of influence
from the US, a lot.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.950
But we also here like my actual wife,

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.510
she's a pop singer in Mexico.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:39.653
- So you gotta say her
then, don't not say her.

00:01:39.653 --> 00:01:40.493
- Say what? Her.

00:01:40.493 --> 00:01:42.120
(crowd laughs)

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.814
- This is the cue where you say her.

00:01:44.814 --> 00:01:47.380
- Her, her, Alessandra Rosaldo.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:50.000
- [Kelly] Oh, that's so
cool, that's awesome.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.150
- What did you listen to growing up?

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.620
- Everything, girl everything.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.628
- Me too.

00:01:53.628 --> 00:01:56.320
- I mean Lauryn Hill to
the Fugees to like Motown-

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:57.350
- [Kelly] Annie Lennox.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.230
- Yeah, everyone and everyone.

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:00.063
- [Kelly] Aretha.

00:02:00.063 --> 00:02:00.896
- Everyone, yeah.

00:02:00.896 --> 00:02:02.760
- Yeah, I feel like we
had like such cool people

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.370
when we were younger to
listen to, I don't know.

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.930
Does everybody feel
like that? I don't know.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.795
Well, John Malcovich is on
your album I find it crazy.

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:11.690
What kind of happenstance was that,

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:12.720
that he ended up on your album?

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.430
- So Pete Berg invited me
to be a part of his movie

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:17.500
called Mile 22.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.480
And we were acting together and you know,

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.440
whatever time off we had,

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.883
he was just talking about
his stories from theater,

00:02:23.883 --> 00:02:27.080
and connected, and he's
my mentor now here.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.347
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:29.180
(crowd claps)

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.440
He's like one of my favorite actors.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.370
- He is the best, he is.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:32.470
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.303
- Yeah.

00:02:33.303 --> 00:02:34.763
- And this is even more random,

00:02:34.763 --> 00:02:36.480
is it true that Mike Tyson

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.744
was an inspiration for this album?

00:02:37.744 --> 00:02:38.577
- [Girl] Yes.

00:02:38.577 --> 00:02:39.410
- [Kelly] Please tell me how.

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.410
- [CL] You know, he's doing
these podcasts these days.

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:42.760
I'm a fan of him to start with-

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:43.593
- [Kelly] Oh I didn't know that.

00:02:43.593 --> 00:02:45.810
- Yeah and I was just
going through his podcast

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.364
and some of the things he said,

00:02:47.364 --> 00:02:49.960
things like before I fight,

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.790
how he feels, I connected to that.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.188
- Oh.

00:02:53.188 --> 00:02:54.052
(CL laughs)

00:02:54.052 --> 00:02:56.833
- Do you see the stage as a boxing arena?

00:02:56.833 --> 00:02:59.076
- You know, I think it's
just about the gap between,

00:02:59.076 --> 00:03:02.452
